    [
     1,
     "<div dir=\"ltr\"><blockquote class=\"gmail_quote\" style=\"margin:0;margin-left:0.8ex;border-left:1px #ccc solid;padding-left:1ex\"><div dir=\"auto\"><div dir=\"auto\"><span style=\"font-family:sans-serif\">not each one separately?</span></div></div></blockquote><div><br></div><div>Oh, you have 2 separate models (one per group).  Instead, fit a multigroup model, then an additional defined parameter that is the difference you are looking for.  You can read the tutorial for the standard way to write multigroup syntax, with vectors of parameter labels (1 per groups):</div><div><br></div><div><a href=\"https://lavaan.ugent.be/tutorial/groups.html\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=https://lavaan.ugent.be/tutorial/groups.html&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792421692187000&amp;usg=AOvVaw3PBYbUKtoTi7ztLSSGVvUg\">https://lavaan.ugent.be/tutorial/groups.html</a><br></div><div><br></div><div>But I think you could also just use the &quot;blocks&quot; structure to utilize the syntax you already wrote.</div><div><br></div><div><div style=\"background-color:rgb(250,250,250);border-color:rgb(187,187,187);border-style:solid;border-width:1px\"><code><div><span style=\"color:#000\">mod </span><span style=\"color:#660\">&lt;-</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> c</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#080\">&#39; group: Control &#39;</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> model</span><span style=\"color:#660\">.</span><span style=\"color:#000\">C</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#080\">&#39; group: Treatment &#39;</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> model</span><span style=\"color:#660\">.</span><span style=\"color:#000\">T</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> <br>         </span><span style=\"color:#080\">&#39; DoubleDiff := SMD.dif.C - SMD.dif.T &#39;</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#660\">)</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br>fit </span><span style=\"color:#660\">&lt;-</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> cfa</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#000\">mod</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> std</span><span style=\"color:#660\">.</span><span style=\"color:#000\">lv </span><span style=\"color:#660\">=</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> TRUE</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br>           sample</span><span style=\"color:#660\">.</span><span style=\"color:#000\">cov </span><span style=\"color:#660\">=</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> list</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#606\">Control</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#660\">=</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#606\">Cov</span><span style=\"color:#660\">.</span><span style=\"color:#000\">C</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#606\">Treatment</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#660\">=</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#606\">Cov</span><span style=\"color:#660\">.</span><span style=\"color:#000\">T</span><span style=\"color:#660\">),</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br>           sample</span><span style=\"color:#660\">.</span><span style=\"color:#000\">mean </span><span style=\"color:#660\">=</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> list</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#606\">Mean</span><span style=\"color:#660\">.</span><span style=\"color:#000\">C</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#606\">Mean</span><span style=\"color:#660\">.</span><span style=\"color:#000\">T</span><span style=\"color:#660\">),</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br>           sample</span><span style=\"color:#660\">.</span><span style=\"color:#000\">nobs</span><span style=\"color:#660\">=</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> list</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#000\">N</span><span style=\"color:#660\">.</span><span style=\"color:#000\">C</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> N</span><span style=\"color:#660\">.</span><span style=\"color:#000\">T</span><span style=\"color:#660\">),</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br>           sample</span><span style=\"color:#660\">.</span><span style=\"color:#000\">cov</span><span style=\"color:#660\">.</span><span style=\"color:#000\">rescale </span><span style=\"color:#660\">=</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> FALSE</span><span style=\"color:#660\">)</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#800\"># why? Is Cov.C already calculated using N.C instead of (N.C - 1)?</span></div></code></div><div style=\"font-family:monospace;background-color:rgb(250,250,250)\"><span style=\"color:rgb(102,102,0)\"><br></span></div></div></div>"
